  "body": "It must be something happening when using a base profile, with the white balance set as \"As Shot\". I tried and the reported problem does not appear when opening the images without a base profile. I checked my base profile and I don't have much there about white balance:\n[White Balance]\nEnabled=true\nSetting=Camera\n\nHere you can see what I get after opening a raw:\n\n<img width=\"409\" height=\"449\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d08aa5a-0291-4458-959e-15b53be3417e\" />\n\nAnd this is what I get if I change WB method and then back to \"As Shot\" (or I change the WB manually):\n\n<img width=\"409\" height=\"279\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3ab23509-52fa-425f-9c30-03949f052bac\" />\n\nBTW, is it correct that, on the R5m2, the only WB methods shown are As Shot, Auto, Custom temperature, and Custom multipliers?\n\nLater I'll try to find a CR3 file that I can provide to you.",
